# BFF endpoints on the local stack (docker compose up --wait), through the gateway.
# Sign in first, headless: scripts/dev-login.sh customer-a
# then copy the disputedesk-session value from the cookie jar it prints into @session below.
# With curl, pass the jar instead: curl -b <cookie-jar> -c <cookie-jar> ...

@app = http://localhost:8080
@session = paste-the-disputedesk-session-cookie-value

### Session state: anonymous without the cookie, unlinked or linked with it
GET {{app}}/api/v1/bff/session
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### Antiforgery token for the X-XSRF-TOKEN header (401 without a session). It also sets the antiforgery cookie.
# @name antiforgery
GET {{app}}/api/v1/bff/antiforgery
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}

### Sign out: 302 to Zitadel's end-session endpoint. Send the antiforgery cookie from the previous response too.
POST {{app}}/api/v1/bff/logout
Cookie: disputedesk-session={{session}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{antiforgery.response.body.requestToken}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

### Sign in in a browser instead: open this URL
GET {{app}}/api/v1/bff/login?returnUrl=/
